.th MTDUMP VI 2/10/77
.sh NAME
mtdump \*- magtape dump
.sh SYNOPSIS
.bd mtdump
[ -eofs ] [ device ]
.sh DESCRIPTION
.it Mtdump
scans through a magtape and produces a summary of the size of blocks
and the positions of tape-marks.
.s3
Device is the unit on which the tape is loaded.
If device is simply a digit, then the string "/dev/rmt"
is prepended to it to obtain the unit.
The default unit is "/dev/rmt0".
.s3
Eofs are the number of tape marks used to represent the end-of-tape.
The default (industry standard) is 2 tape-marks.
Unix only uses 1 tape-mark.
.s3
The example below will dump a CYBER tape (with all its tape marks)
on drive 1.

	mtdump -4 1

.sh FILES
.nf
.if t .ta 1.2i
.if n .ta 14
/dev/rmt?	for input
.fi
.dt
.sh DIAGNOSTICS
cant open file; self explanatory.
.sh AUTHOR
Craig McGregor (University of New South Wales)
.sh BUGS
